WEBVTT

01:33.201 --> 01:35.801
(Adapted from the web novel "Waiting for You in a City")

01:36.070 --> 01:38.001
(Fireworks of My Heart)

01:38.240 --> 01:41.010
(Episode 16)

01:41.540 --> 01:44.341
Lately, we've exposed a lot of weaknesses in our rescue operations.

01:45.380 --> 01:46.781
Especially medical rescues.

01:48.320 --> 01:51.490
How do you all feel? Let's talk about it.

01:51.650 --> 01:52.551
Sir.

01:53.520 --> 01:54.490
Here's the thing.

01:54.891 --> 01:56.421
Simple dressings to stop the bleeding...

01:56.490 --> 01:57.620
are not a problem for us.

01:57.721 --> 01:58.490
- Right? - Yes.

01:58.561 --> 02:00.091
But when it's more complicated,

02:00.161 --> 02:01.501
we don't have the know-how.

02:01.900 --> 02:04.600
Besides, it's not our main job...

02:04.661 --> 02:06.031
as firefighters to treat injuries.

02:06.301 --> 02:07.570
It's mainly because we don't know how.

02:08.301 --> 02:10.441
- Sir, Chief. I have an idea. - Go ahead.

02:10.501 --> 02:13.111
Can we discuss this with the medical unit?

02:13.171 --> 02:15.281
Fire engines and ambulances arrive at the scene together.

02:15.811 --> 02:17.341
Only when professional doctors and nurses are present...

02:17.411 --> 02:19.550
can the injured receive immediate help.

02:19.811 --> 02:20.510
Instructor.

02:21.251 --> 02:23.580
We thought about Da Peng's idea before.

02:24.580 --> 02:26.350
For example, when there are injured people at the scene,

02:26.420 --> 02:27.390
we'll call 120.

02:27.450 --> 02:28.290
That's not a problem.

02:28.820 --> 02:30.461
But having an ambulance on standby at all times...

02:30.521 --> 02:31.661
and going with us in operations...

02:31.730 --> 02:32.591
does not seem realistic either.

02:32.991 --> 02:34.390
After all, we don't belong to the same system.

02:34.860 --> 02:36.130
That's the same as saying nothing.

02:36.860 --> 02:37.931
You're right.

02:39.271 --> 02:40.170
What do you think?

02:42.170 --> 02:44.540
Rescue scenes are complicated situations.

02:45.070 --> 02:46.941
It's not hard to come up with ideas.

02:47.941 --> 02:48.811
What's hard is implementation.

02:51.580 --> 02:53.050
Do the hard thing and you'll get something.

02:55.021 --> 02:55.781
I'd like to try it.

03:01.350 --> 03:02.661
Time to train. Come on.

03:02.860 --> 03:03.820
Get going.

03:04.760 --> 03:05.461
It's too hot.

03:05.760 --> 03:06.461
Let's go.

03:12.371 --> 03:14.471
(Application for Joint Firefighting and Medical Rescue Team)

03:14.800 --> 03:17.800
Set up a joint firefighting, medical, and rescue team.

03:19.941 --> 03:21.441
Is this a spur-of-the-moment idea...

03:21.781 --> 03:23.211
or have you been thinking about it for a long time?

03:24.441 --> 03:25.350
Commissar.

03:25.411 --> 03:27.311
During the fire in the shantytown,

03:27.651 --> 03:31.251
the person who called for help said that it was uninhabited...

03:31.320 --> 03:32.320
and was set for demolition.

03:32.651 --> 03:33.751
But when we got there,

03:33.820 --> 03:36.161
we found a child who was severely injured.

03:37.121 --> 03:39.461
We gave her emergency treatment...

03:39.730 --> 03:40.860
and sent her to the hospital.

03:41.661 --> 03:43.100
A few days ago,

03:43.161 --> 03:44.800
we found a hiker who was badly injured...

03:44.871 --> 03:45.830
in the mountains.

03:45.971 --> 03:48.971
We had to use the satellite phone to ask a doctor for help.

03:50.200 --> 03:52.110
I was deeply moved by these two incidents.

03:52.441 --> 03:55.241
If we had medical staff on our team,

03:55.380 --> 03:58.480
we could've handled the crisis more quickly and efficiently.

03:59.350 --> 04:01.080
We could also drastically reduce the casualty rate.

04:02.080 --> 04:03.521
That's what I've been thinking lately...

04:03.980 --> 04:05.651
and a long-term goal of mine.

04:07.850 --> 04:11.061
Yes, it would be best for doctors to treat patients at the scene.

04:13.191 --> 04:14.931
It's just that medical care...

04:15.001 --> 04:17.061
and firefighting are under two departments.

04:17.730 --> 04:18.931
When they work together,

04:19.001 --> 04:20.531
time gaps cannot be avoided.

04:20.771 --> 04:22.741
But it's all within our control.

04:23.771 --> 04:27.211
If we can train doctors for rescue missions...

04:27.370 --> 04:29.581
and at the same time strengthen cooperation...

04:29.781 --> 04:30.680
between the two departments,

04:30.740 --> 04:31.680
that's also a good thing.

04:34.180 --> 04:36.321
Your suggestion is not bad.

04:36.821 --> 04:37.721
However,

04:37.980 --> 04:41.321
doctors and firefighters will go to ground zero together.

04:41.420 --> 04:42.961
This is no joke.

04:43.060 --> 04:46.060
How do we improve their resilience on the scene...

04:46.131 --> 04:47.891
while also ensuring their safety?

04:48.930 --> 04:49.800
Have you thought about it?

04:50.331 --> 04:54.170
Have firefighters target-train medical staff...

04:54.230 --> 04:56.040
and set safety guidelines.

04:57.901 --> 05:00.940
It seems like you already have a plan for the training.

05:02.240 --> 05:03.110
Right.

05:05.550 --> 05:07.180
Commissar, I prepared the proposal.

05:17.620 --> 05:19.230
You're well-prepared.

05:20.930 --> 05:23.761
You were so keen to work at the grassroots level.

05:24.060 --> 05:25.370
I was afraid you wouldn't get used to it.

05:26.701 --> 05:28.740
How is it? Is it going well with Song Yan?

05:28.800 --> 05:30.141
He has been a great help to me.

05:30.571 --> 05:31.810
He's also very supportive.

05:33.940 --> 05:35.581
I know his temper best.

05:35.881 --> 05:38.141
It's not easy for you two to work together.

05:40.980 --> 05:41.951
Okay.

05:42.651 --> 05:45.790
I'll submit your proposal to the higher-ups.

05:46.250 --> 05:49.190
I'll try to make Shilitai a trial unit...

05:49.261 --> 05:50.661
to work with the municipal hospital.

05:50.761 --> 05:51.560
Thank you, Commissar.

05:54.391 --> 05:56.201
Thank you all for coming.

05:56.261 --> 05:58.771
I wish our two departments a successful collaboration.

05:59.170 --> 06:02.500
Also, I hope you consider doing the media coverage.

06:02.641 --> 06:03.971
It's publicity after all.

06:04.540 --> 06:06.170
Thank you, Mr. Liu. Goodbye.

06:06.670 --> 06:07.341
See you again.

06:13.180 --> 06:14.581
It's all about appearances.

06:15.120 --> 06:17.281
As long as it doesn't affect the actual job.

06:17.451 --> 06:18.591
What job?

06:19.420 --> 06:22.321
I've always been against forming a joint rescue team.

06:22.521 --> 06:23.821
My opinion remains unchanged.

06:24.161 --> 06:26.290
Doctors and nurses don't know enough about fire scenes.

06:26.560 --> 06:28.060
They are incapable of handling them.

06:28.190 --> 06:30.600
We're not telling them to go into the fire.

06:30.901 --> 06:32.201
I'll train them well.

06:33.100 --> 06:34.430
They'll be fine with the safety guidelines, right?

06:34.800 --> 06:35.940
It's easy for you to say.

06:36.401 --> 06:37.641
Do doctors and nurses...

06:37.740 --> 06:39.641
work at the hospital or fire station?

06:40.411 --> 06:42.781
When hospital work and firefighting work clash,

06:42.841 --> 06:43.841
which side should they prioritize?

06:44.980 --> 06:46.350
That's why I say...

06:47.110 --> 06:48.250
you're full of fantasies.

06:48.651 --> 06:49.980
It's not wishful thinking.

06:50.321 --> 06:51.420
First, let's do a trial run.

06:51.480 --> 06:53.990
We'll get some medical professionals to work with the firefighters.

06:54.050 --> 06:55.161
That's good, right?

06:55.521 --> 06:56.360
You're going off course now.

06:56.420 --> 06:57.420
Let's get back on track then.

06:57.661 --> 07:00.161
You can give me some pointers when I get the team set up.

07:01.060 --> 07:01.800
I'm sorry.

07:05.300 --> 07:05.971
What a coincidence.

07:09.141 --> 07:10.100
What are you doing here?

07:11.240 --> 07:14.011
We're here because of the joint rescue team.

07:14.641 --> 07:15.540
Let me introduce you.

07:15.610 --> 07:16.781
Song Yan, our station chief.

07:22.651 --> 07:23.620
Do you know each other?

07:24.321 --> 07:25.091
- No. - Yes.

07:27.620 --> 07:28.620
- Sort of. - No.

07:32.461 --> 07:34.161
You two carry on. I'll get going.

07:39.170 --> 07:40.031
What was that about?

07:42.740 --> 07:43.540
None of your business.

07:46.740 --> 07:48.071
Don't you want to know...

07:48.610 --> 07:50.040
how I met her?

07:51.211 --> 07:52.081
It's none of my business.

07:53.480 --> 07:54.180
Fine.

07:54.250 --> 07:55.250
Please.

07:55.680 --> 07:57.521
The report will be ready in five days.

07:58.690 --> 07:59.920
- Thank you. - Don't mention it.

07:59.990 --> 08:00.721
Take care, Mr. Meng.

08:07.961 --> 08:10.560
(I'll wait for you downstairs)

08:32.651 --> 08:33.420
Yan Chen.

08:35.161 --> 08:36.120
Are you done with your checkup?

08:36.620 --> 08:37.521
What do you want for lunch?

08:38.290 --> 08:39.331
Why didn't you get changed?

08:40.090 --> 08:41.590
I'll just eat in the cafeteria.

08:43.101 --> 08:44.901
I wanted to take you out for something good.

08:45.501 --> 08:46.200
Yan Chen.

08:46.401 --> 08:47.601
I'm very busy, okay?

08:51.040 --> 08:52.470
Is our cafeteria too lousy for you?

08:53.141 --> 08:54.040
That's not it.

08:54.271 --> 08:55.540
It's okay to try it out.

08:56.381 --> 08:57.141
Do you remember?

08:57.481 --> 08:58.810
You were always hungry when you were little.

08:59.080 --> 09:00.651
I always took you out secretly to eat.

09:01.710 --> 09:02.521
I don't remember.

09:03.521 --> 09:04.521
You don't?

09:10.060 --> 09:10.920
You have to support me.

09:12.991 --> 09:13.891
We meet again.

09:16.800 --> 09:17.901
Why are you at the hospital?

09:22.101 --> 09:23.300
For a checkup.

09:23.440 --> 09:24.300
And you?

09:24.440 --> 09:25.440
For work.

09:26.241 --> 09:27.340
Let me introduce you.

09:28.070 --> 09:28.810
Song Yan.

09:28.940 --> 09:30.241
He's the chief of our fire station.

09:30.611 --> 09:31.440
Meng Yan Chen.

09:32.050 --> 09:32.881
Xu Qin's older brother.

09:38.851 --> 09:39.621
Do you know each other?

09:40.021 --> 09:40.851
- I don't know him. - I don't know him.

09:42.690 --> 09:43.761
Get to know each other then.

09:49.330 --> 09:50.131
Hello.

09:52.901 --> 09:53.771
Hello.

09:58.300 --> 09:59.040
Let's go, Yan Chen.

09:59.771 --> 10:00.470
We're leaving.

10:26.601 --> 10:27.570
Mr. Liu.

10:28.840 --> 10:29.601
Madam Fu.

10:29.970 --> 10:32.340
Song Yan is now the chief of the fire station.

10:37.011 --> 10:38.141
I don't know him.

10:42.621 --> 10:44.720
Right. You don't know him.

10:45.121 --> 10:45.920
I misspoke.

10:46.420 --> 10:47.290
It's nothing.

11:16.881 --> 11:18.790
(Yanbei Fire and Rescue Detachment)

11:24.021 --> 11:25.220
Take your time.

11:25.290 --> 11:26.361
Take a good look.

11:27.761 --> 11:29.601
This is about the hospital's reputation.

11:31.361 --> 11:32.401
It's also an opportunity...

11:32.470 --> 11:33.601
for the Emergency Department to shine.

11:39.111 --> 11:40.871
I know you don't care.

11:41.741 --> 11:42.981
But it's a good opportunity...

11:43.040 --> 11:44.440
for the young people in your department.

11:50.021 --> 11:51.621
If you have any opinions, just say it.

11:54.320 --> 11:55.861
I don't think it's appropriate...

11:56.090 --> 11:58.521
for doctors to live and train at the fire station.

11:59.330 --> 12:01.631
Also, the doctors have to go to ground zero.

12:01.690 --> 12:03.501
Conditions there would be complicated.

12:04.300 --> 12:05.901
Who can guarantee the doctors' safety?

12:11.570 --> 12:13.840
Those two things coincide.

12:14.771 --> 12:16.810
How can we guarantee a doctor's safety on ground zero?

12:17.210 --> 12:19.080
Shouldn't he have proper coping knowledge?

12:19.381 --> 12:20.580
How do we do that?

12:20.810 --> 12:22.680
Isn't it through training?

12:23.180 --> 12:25.121
If you don't train, how are you going to treat patients?

12:28.521 --> 12:30.320
That's not what you should think about.

12:30.621 --> 12:32.491
Just think about who you should choose.

12:33.361 --> 12:34.131
No need to think.

12:36.700 --> 12:37.460
Send me.

12:39.731 --> 12:40.771
I'm not kidding with you.

12:41.371 --> 12:43.141
I'm telling you, it's a missive from Mr. Wang.

12:43.340 --> 12:45.170
If you have a problem with it, take it up with him.

13:03.320 --> 13:04.920
(The setting up of a joint rescue team)

13:07.531 --> 13:09.361
Sir, I'd like to go.

13:11.361 --> 13:12.300
What's your reason?

13:13.371 --> 13:15.001
Someone in our department has to go.

13:15.371 --> 13:17.501
Whether at the hospital or at the rescue scene,

13:17.570 --> 13:18.440
it's about saving lives.

13:18.810 --> 13:20.170
The doctor's duty remains unchanged.

13:20.470 --> 13:21.611
Do you really think so?

13:24.210 --> 13:26.281
Okay, I understand.

13:29.381 --> 13:31.281
I'll get back to work then, sir.

13:31.851 --> 13:32.751
Okay.

13:48.430 --> 13:49.700
- Li Nan. - Dr. Xu.

13:51.901 --> 13:53.741
I thought you didn't want to go to the rescue team.

13:54.940 --> 13:55.641
I'm sorry.

13:56.210 --> 13:59.050
I made the decision without discussing it with the team.

13:59.611 --> 14:00.351
It's okay.

14:00.680 --> 14:02.720
The hospital has already decided to let our team go.

14:04.781 --> 14:06.651
Okay, I'll let you pack up. I'll get going.

14:07.420 --> 14:08.420
- Bye. - Bye.

14:21.970 --> 14:23.371
Why did you want to see me today?

14:25.570 --> 14:26.710
I came to say goodbye.

14:27.411 --> 14:29.580
I'm leaving in two days.

14:29.881 --> 14:32.411
My plan is to travel for half a year.

14:32.611 --> 14:34.810
If I have fun, I'll go to West Africa next.

14:35.050 --> 14:35.820
You're really leaving?

14:38.080 --> 14:39.651
You're really spontaneous.

14:39.720 --> 14:42.220
I'm just enjoying life.

14:45.460 --> 14:46.891
I really envy you sometimes.

14:47.131 --> 14:48.290
You can do it too.

14:54.131 --> 14:55.700
How are things between you and him?

14:57.101 --> 14:57.840
In the past,

14:58.040 --> 14:59.340
I didn't want to hurt him.

15:00.940 --> 15:04.340
But now, holding myself back is not only hurting him...

15:04.411 --> 15:05.781
but also hurting myself too.

15:07.481 --> 15:09.481
I used to think that if I wanted it,

15:10.050 --> 15:11.050
he wouldn't leave.

15:11.420 --> 15:12.351
But now...

15:12.420 --> 15:14.050
It's all on you.

15:16.361 --> 15:17.060
Maybe.

15:18.460 --> 15:19.731
Maybe it's my instinct...

15:20.560 --> 15:22.261
to keep wanting to test his limits.

15:25.670 --> 15:26.401
Maybe...

15:27.570 --> 15:29.141
Is it possible that just like what he said,

15:29.241 --> 15:30.641
you only decided to go back to him...

15:30.700 --> 15:33.340
because you didn't find anyone new?

15:34.771 --> 15:35.781
I don't know.

15:36.481 --> 15:38.011
Sometimes, I wonder...

15:38.540 --> 15:40.481
if I've lost the ability to love someone.

15:41.180 --> 15:42.820
That's why I'm stuck in the memories.

15:43.851 --> 15:45.180
But no matter how much I say it,

15:45.790 --> 15:46.851
when it comes to it,

15:48.960 --> 15:50.290
I still don't want to give up.

15:50.720 --> 15:51.861
It's Song Yan we're talking about.

15:51.920 --> 15:52.960
Who would give him up?

15:53.491 --> 15:54.590
So what are you going to do?

15:55.930 --> 15:57.330
He took one step towards me.

15:57.800 --> 15:58.700
So I'll take a step towards him.

15:59.470 --> 16:00.531
Just like what he said,

16:01.231 --> 16:02.570
he doesn't know who I am now.

16:03.241 --> 16:04.401
He doesn't know if the present me...

16:04.570 --> 16:05.940
is worthy of his love.

16:07.170 --> 16:08.040
As for me,

16:08.340 --> 16:09.641
I don't know who he is now either.

16:10.440 --> 16:11.680
I don't know if I like...

16:12.141 --> 16:13.611
who he is now.

16:14.611 --> 16:15.511
So?

16:17.281 --> 16:18.420
We'll get to know each other again.

16:51.021 --> 16:53.891
They are doctors and nurses from the municipal hospital.

16:53.950 --> 16:57.460
They are the ones who came to Shilitai...

16:57.521 --> 16:59.531
as part of the new joint rescue team.

16:59.590 --> 17:01.090
Let's give them a round of applause.

17:05.930 --> 17:07.101
Let me introduce myself.

17:07.731 --> 17:09.540
I'm Jiang Yu, the instructor.

17:10.141 --> 17:12.440
He's Song Yan, the station chief.

17:13.371 --> 17:14.041
Hello.

17:16.541 --> 17:19.010
Let's introduce ourselves and get acquainted.

17:20.651 --> 17:21.351
Hello, everyone.

17:21.411 --> 17:24.351
I'm Xu Xi, an ER nurse.

17:24.420 --> 17:25.920
I look forward to working with you.

17:27.351 --> 17:28.020
Hello, everyone.

17:28.091 --> 17:29.891
I'm an ER nurse, Chen Dong Dong.

17:31.960 --> 17:34.490
Hello, I'm an ER doctor, Xu Qin.

17:38.460 --> 17:40.631
Hello, I'm an ER doctor, Li Nan.

17:43.000 --> 17:45.301
Hello, everyone. I'm an ER nurse, Feng Bei.

17:47.341 --> 17:49.611
Let's welcome once again Dr. Xu Qin...

17:49.680 --> 17:51.440
and her medical team.

18:02.291 --> 18:03.861
Nice to meet you, Chief Song.

18:07.760 --> 18:09.301
Nice to meet you, Dr. Xu.

18:12.000 --> 18:12.871
This way, please.

18:13.331 --> 18:14.301
Welcome, everyone.

18:14.700 --> 18:16.301
- A warm welcome. - Welcome them warmly.

18:20.010 --> 18:20.940
Louder!

18:21.010 --> 18:21.770
Please come in.

18:22.170 --> 18:22.980
Hip hip, hooray!

18:23.611 --> 18:24.911
This is our dormitory.

18:24.980 --> 18:26.581
Feel free to look around.

18:27.051 --> 18:30.381
This men's dormitory is incredibly neat.

18:31.250 --> 18:34.851
It's completely different from our on-call room.

18:35.321 --> 18:36.121
You're one to talk.

18:36.220 --> 18:37.161
It's all because of you.

18:38.760 --> 18:41.061
So I heard you don't take off your socks when you sleep.

18:41.131 --> 18:41.990
Is that true?

18:42.361 --> 18:43.401
It's not that exaggerated.

18:43.601 --> 18:44.730
But when the alarm goes off,

18:44.801 --> 18:45.631
no matter what you're doing,

18:45.700 --> 18:46.530
you put on your shoes and go.

18:47.770 --> 18:49.301
It must be pretty tough.

18:50.970 --> 18:52.101
By the way,

18:52.240 --> 18:54.141
don't you guys have any miscellaneous stuff?

18:54.371 --> 18:55.311
We do.

18:55.371 --> 18:56.980
We keep them in the cabinet.

19:05.680 --> 19:08.291
Well, that Pan Pan sticker is pretty cute.

19:11.960 --> 19:12.661
Da Peng.

19:13.331 --> 19:14.460
Why are your ears red?

19:14.530 --> 19:15.391
Are you embarrassed?

19:15.760 --> 19:16.561
No.

19:16.901 --> 19:18.730
We're just checking out your dorm.

19:18.801 --> 19:20.230
There's nothing to be embarrassed about.

19:20.970 --> 19:22.101
Quite the pure soul you are.

19:22.641 --> 19:23.970
How about this?

19:24.170 --> 19:25.000
Let's continue the tour.

19:25.541 --> 19:26.641
- Send them off. - Farewell.

19:27.210 --> 19:28.170
This way.

19:32.240 --> 19:33.710
Let's go to the front. This way.

19:37.180 --> 19:38.051
What's this?

19:40.220 --> 19:40.920
This?

19:41.291 --> 19:43.621
This is for convenience when we leave for emergency responses.

19:43.690 --> 19:45.220
It's a product of the history of firefighting.

19:45.291 --> 19:47.430
It's also a relic from the fire brigade days.

19:47.530 --> 19:49.061
But now, for safety reasons,

19:49.131 --> 19:50.000
we don't use it anymore.

19:50.061 --> 19:52.401
Yes. But we can give you a demonstration.

19:53.930 --> 19:56.000
Jiang Yi, you don't have to do it.

19:56.101 --> 19:57.440
You have a leg injury. Let me.

19:57.500 --> 19:58.301
My leg is fine now.

19:58.371 --> 19:59.411
It's fine. I'll do it.

19:59.740 --> 20:00.470
It has to be me.

20:00.970 --> 20:01.740
Well...

20:02.740 --> 20:03.980
You guys take the stairs.

20:04.041 --> 20:05.041
See you downstairs.

20:05.141 --> 20:05.851
Safety first.

20:06.680 --> 20:07.710
Bye.

20:12.081 --> 20:13.051
That's so cool.

20:13.391 --> 20:14.250
Is that cool?

20:14.490 --> 20:15.651
We used to do this every day.

20:15.821 --> 20:18.091
Jiang Yi, what's wrong with praising me?

20:18.960 --> 20:20.490
All right. You're the coolest.

20:20.631 --> 20:21.361
Of course.

20:21.530 --> 20:23.601
Can we try this?

20:23.801 --> 20:24.530
No.

20:24.861 --> 20:27.601
Only veterans who are professionally trained can use this.

20:27.901 --> 20:29.030
Not even we learned how to do it.

20:29.541 --> 20:30.500
Let's take the stairs. It's safe.

20:30.571 --> 20:31.301
Follow me.

20:35.041 --> 20:35.980
This way.

20:49.020 --> 20:49.720
Dr. Xu.

20:50.121 --> 20:51.121
Go down that way.

20:55.260 --> 20:57.401
Dr. Xu. It's Open Day today.

20:57.460 --> 20:59.530
Come in and take a look if you're curious.

21:00.331 --> 21:02.641
Everywhere else is open, but not my room.

21:03.041 --> 21:04.601
It's my room too.

21:04.740 --> 21:06.010
I have half the right to use it.

21:09.581 --> 21:10.411
Come on.

21:14.151 --> 21:15.180
Must you argue with me?

21:15.250 --> 21:16.180
I'm not.

21:17.680 --> 21:18.821
Come on, take a look around.

21:21.891 --> 21:22.561
What do you think?

21:22.920 --> 21:25.460
Guess which of the beds belongs to Song Yan.

21:26.990 --> 21:27.661
This one.

21:29.760 --> 21:31.131
You're good. They're exactly the same.

21:31.200 --> 21:32.131
How did you guess?

21:32.200 --> 21:33.700
There's a photo on it.

21:35.401 --> 21:36.141
Not bad.

21:50.651 --> 21:52.081
Is he the one you like?

21:55.520 --> 21:57.561
That stubborn dude. He pretended not to know you.

21:58.720 --> 22:00.490
- About us... - What about us?

22:01.061 --> 22:03.061
You mean that my parents know your parents?

22:13.371 --> 22:16.280
One, two, three, four.

22:16.541 --> 22:19.351
- One, two, three, four. - One, two, three, four.

22:19.551 --> 22:21.911
One, two, one, halt.

22:23.680 --> 22:25.420
Everyone, right turn.

22:25.680 --> 22:26.821
Eyes right.

22:29.361 --> 22:30.661
Eyes front.

22:31.321 --> 22:33.230
Reporting. The medical team has assembled.

22:38.131 --> 22:39.101
The training suit has to change.

22:42.000 --> 22:43.301
- Da Peng. - Yes, sir.

22:43.801 --> 22:44.901
Tally the sizes.

22:45.000 --> 22:45.841
Yes, sir.

22:51.440 --> 22:52.280
First of all,

22:53.280 --> 22:56.121
I'd like to welcome the medical staff.

22:56.621 --> 22:58.750
Thank you for joining the station...

22:58.821 --> 23:01.351
and working with us to try new rescue methods.

23:02.020 --> 23:02.690
Secondly,

23:02.760 --> 23:06.760
we conduct some basic training on your physical fitness.

23:06.990 --> 23:11.960
The main purpose is to make rescues more efficient.

23:12.401 --> 23:14.401
To respond to crises quicker...

23:14.530 --> 23:18.371
and be flexible and agile at the scene.

23:18.440 --> 23:19.240
One more thing.

23:19.740 --> 23:22.780
It's to make rescue operations more coordinated,

23:23.480 --> 23:24.280
more efficient.

23:24.411 --> 23:27.551
(Yancheng Fire and Rescue, Yanbei Detachment)

23:31.420 --> 23:32.520
I'm only going to say three things.

23:32.920 --> 23:33.851
Number one.

23:33.920 --> 23:35.821
Team members must obey orders.

23:36.690 --> 23:37.891
Emergency scenes are complicated.

23:38.220 --> 23:39.260
When you arrive at the scene,

23:39.430 --> 23:41.661
you must obey the commander's delegation.

23:41.960 --> 23:43.661
Obeying orders and following instructions...

23:43.730 --> 23:46.401
are the prerequisites for completing any rescue operation.

23:46.670 --> 23:47.670
Second,

23:47.831 --> 23:51.401
safety always comes first before entering any site.

23:52.541 --> 23:53.240
Three.

23:54.141 --> 23:56.081
Due to the conditions of your physical strength,

23:56.841 --> 23:59.950
you must not put your own lives at risk.

24:01.381 --> 24:02.311
Do you understand?

24:02.381 --> 24:03.720
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

24:05.551 --> 24:06.450
Let's begin.

24:06.520 --> 24:07.490
Medical team, all present.

24:07.891 --> 24:08.551
On my mark.

24:08.821 --> 24:09.960
Turn left.

24:11.260 --> 24:12.661
Double time, march.

24:13.561 --> 24:14.591
All present.

24:15.391 --> 24:16.460
Turn right.

24:17.530 --> 24:18.561
Double time, march.

24:21.530 --> 24:22.700
One, two, one.

24:24.141 --> 24:25.341
One, two, one.

24:30.881 --> 24:36.581
(Braving fire and water, Always ready to fight and win)

24:38.081 --> 24:40.291
- Dr. Xu, I have to check the size. - Okay.

24:40.351 --> 24:41.220
What's your shoe size?

24:41.321 --> 24:42.020
Thirty-seven.

24:42.091 --> 24:42.920
Thirty-seven.

24:43.490 --> 24:44.891
What's your shirt and pants size?

24:44.960 --> 24:45.821
Size M.

24:47.061 --> 24:47.960
Okay, thank you.

24:48.161 --> 24:48.861
No problem.

24:52.601 --> 24:53.301
Thank you.

24:58.041 --> 24:58.700
Thank you.

25:01.270 --> 25:03.740
These tasks are a bit difficult for you.

25:06.581 --> 25:07.611
Are you looking down on me?

25:09.010 --> 25:10.081
In the past, you'd catch a cold...

25:10.321 --> 25:11.520
just because you sweated a little.

25:11.821 --> 25:12.851
You're so weak.

25:12.990 --> 25:14.051
You should be in the hospital.

25:14.450 --> 25:15.551
Why are you here?

25:16.490 --> 25:18.720
I'm no longer the weak Xu Qin from the past.

25:25.930 --> 25:27.170
Are you worried about me?

25:30.940 --> 25:31.841
All I can think of...

25:32.141 --> 25:33.571
is that there are a lot of emergencies out there.

25:33.841 --> 25:34.841
Situations are complicated.

25:35.210 --> 25:36.041
During the rescue,

25:36.411 --> 25:38.180
I won't have time to look after you all.

25:39.651 --> 25:40.980
You're the head of the medical team.

25:41.510 --> 25:42.510
Didn't you think about that?

25:42.710 --> 25:43.480
I did.

25:43.780 --> 25:45.250
But things rarely go as planned.

25:45.520 --> 25:46.450
In many instances,

25:46.520 --> 25:49.490
100 percent compatibility is impossible from the get-go.

25:49.960 --> 25:52.091
Only by discovering problems and resolving them along the way...

25:52.661 --> 25:54.331
are you able to get the desired result.

25:54.661 --> 25:56.301
Isn't it better to avoid potential risks...

25:56.730 --> 25:58.760
before the problem arises?

26:01.930 --> 26:03.341
It's risky for doctors to go to the scene.

26:03.770 --> 26:05.940
Are there no risks for firefighters?

26:07.371 --> 26:08.470
You're in charge of the rescue.

26:08.571 --> 26:09.611
We're in charge of treatment.

26:10.240 --> 26:12.280
Everyone has their own mission and responsibility.

26:12.851 --> 26:13.950
As long as we work together,

26:14.210 --> 26:16.321
we'll be comrades who fight side by side.

26:17.020 --> 26:18.321
No one is a burden to the other.

26:23.891 --> 26:24.861
Dr. Xu.

26:25.561 --> 26:26.831
You seem to have become braver.

26:28.960 --> 26:30.331
You can omit the word "seem".

26:42.371 --> 26:43.341
I'm done.

26:46.210 --> 26:47.611
I'm done eating. I'm leaving too.

26:52.420 --> 26:53.851
Chief, I'm leaving.

27:13.611 --> 27:14.411
All these years,

27:14.940 --> 27:16.581
the speed at which you eat hasn't changed at all.

27:17.541 --> 27:19.611
You didn't learn what I taught you at all.

27:30.561 --> 27:31.260
Don't waste.

27:32.720 --> 27:33.760
I can't eat anymore.

27:36.161 --> 27:37.200
You didn't eat much.

27:37.601 --> 27:38.500
That's not enough energy.

27:38.930 --> 27:40.331
You need stamina to be a doctor.

27:40.770 --> 27:42.801
It's not good if you don't eat enough.

28:41.161 --> 28:43.601
(Bathrooms, Changing Rooms)

28:48.730 --> 28:50.301
Today, I can give you two a handicap.

28:50.541 --> 28:51.901
- No need. - Stop right there.

28:53.641 --> 28:55.041
Any orders, Class Monitor?

28:55.371 --> 28:56.170
Where are you three going?

28:56.581 --> 28:58.341
We're going to the club room to play basketball.

28:59.081 --> 29:00.411
Play basketball?

29:00.980 --> 29:02.280
- Ge Zheng. - Yes.

29:02.581 --> 29:03.551
Come here.

29:09.651 --> 29:10.661
Stand here.

29:11.420 --> 29:12.361
Stand here?

29:12.661 --> 29:13.460
Stand guard here.

29:13.760 --> 29:16.500
Once the medical team members are done showering,

29:16.661 --> 29:17.801
you can let the others in.

29:19.101 --> 29:19.801
I stand guard?

29:19.930 --> 29:20.700
I don't think that's a good idea.

29:20.770 --> 29:21.901
What's wrong with that?

29:22.801 --> 29:25.101
Chief said the station facilities are limited.

29:25.401 --> 29:26.841
Your standing here...

29:26.911 --> 29:28.841
is to let people know there are people inside.

29:30.641 --> 29:31.341
Okay.

29:34.851 --> 29:35.710
Complete the mission.

29:37.780 --> 29:39.651
- Let's go. I'll play with you guys. - Let's go.

29:54.401 --> 29:56.000
(Bathrooms, Changing Rooms)

29:58.740 --> 30:00.641
- You scared me. - Who is it?

30:01.041 --> 30:01.911
What...

30:02.270 --> 30:03.440
Why are you standing here?

30:05.541 --> 30:06.510
Class...

30:06.581 --> 30:09.450
The class monitor told me to stand here.

30:09.510 --> 30:10.520
He's probably on guard.

30:11.920 --> 30:12.980
Standing guard?

30:13.450 --> 30:15.250
Yes, stand guard.

30:16.520 --> 30:18.061
There's no one else inside.

30:18.621 --> 30:19.420
Thank you for your hard work.

30:19.891 --> 30:20.730
You've worked hard.

30:21.331 --> 30:22.391
We didn't work hard.

30:22.530 --> 30:23.331
You've worked hard.

30:23.561 --> 30:25.530
What have you worked hard for?

30:26.331 --> 30:28.500
Go shower quickly. Then go back and rest.

30:30.141 --> 30:30.801
Okay.

30:31.841 --> 30:32.901
You've worked hard.

30:35.010 --> 30:37.141
Why are the people at the station so shy?

30:37.411 --> 30:38.680
Let's shower faster next time.

30:39.680 --> 30:40.950
They're making me feel bad.

30:51.561 --> 30:52.520
Chief Song.

30:53.990 --> 30:55.190
What is your feedback...

30:55.960 --> 30:56.930
on today's training?

30:59.061 --> 30:59.970
Feedback?

31:01.530 --> 31:02.530
I wouldn't call it feedback.

31:03.240 --> 31:04.200
But I have some ideas.

31:04.740 --> 31:05.500
What ideas?

31:07.611 --> 31:08.371
I'm thinking.

31:09.240 --> 31:11.581
You said the fire station has to target-train...

31:11.641 --> 31:12.980
the accompanying doctors...

31:13.980 --> 31:15.611
and establish field safety guidelines.

31:16.881 --> 31:18.581
But since we're a joint rescue team,

31:18.881 --> 31:20.621
the doctors aren't our sidekicks.

31:21.821 --> 31:22.520
Actually,

31:22.920 --> 31:26.530
we need the doctors to provide us with professional assistance.

31:27.331 --> 31:28.530
They can also...

31:29.091 --> 31:30.930
train us in medical knowledge.

31:32.161 --> 31:33.700
I agree with what you said.

31:34.601 --> 31:36.430
It's a win-win situation if we learn from each other.

31:38.740 --> 31:41.811
That's the poster child of Shilitai for you.

31:46.081 --> 31:46.950
Are you mocking me?

31:48.280 --> 31:49.920
Why can't you just accept a compliment?

31:50.250 --> 31:51.980
Isn't a poster child just for show?

31:52.581 --> 31:53.891
I'm really curious.

31:54.190 --> 31:56.720
Why do you keep obsessing over these small details?

31:57.661 --> 31:59.821
Fine, you're the sexy brain.

31:59.960 --> 32:01.591
I'll be the poster child, okay?

32:03.500 --> 32:04.301
Thank you.

32:04.760 --> 32:05.661
That's what I like to hear.

32:20.480 --> 32:21.510
Is anyone in?

32:29.960 --> 32:30.891
Pan Pan.

32:33.990 --> 32:35.161
These are the new training suits.

32:35.490 --> 32:38.500
If the sizes don't fit, you can come to me.

32:38.561 --> 32:39.500
Okay, thank you.

32:40.301 --> 32:42.631
Also, my name is Zhan Da Peng.

32:43.401 --> 32:44.740
Hello, I'm Li Nan.

32:47.270 --> 32:48.141
I'll get going.

32:48.341 --> 32:49.041
Okay.

32:57.420 --> 32:58.651
How embarrassing.

33:12.000 --> 33:13.331
What else do we have today?

33:13.770 --> 33:16.801
Remember you had to leave early during your checkup?

33:16.940 --> 33:18.170
You still have to do two examinations.

33:19.841 --> 33:21.041
- Okay. - Right.

33:22.240 --> 33:23.240
Last time,

33:23.641 --> 33:24.740
you asked me to book...

33:25.480 --> 33:26.411
a ticket for the exhibition.

33:34.250 --> 33:35.220
Right.

33:35.321 --> 33:36.760
I met someone...

33:36.821 --> 33:39.821
who wishes to get a part-time job at Qinghe Art Museum.

33:40.030 --> 33:40.960
Help introduce them.

33:41.260 --> 33:42.791
I'll send you the contact information later.

33:42.930 --> 33:43.930
All right.

33:44.131 --> 33:46.000
I'll go now if there's nothing else.

33:51.901 --> 33:54.210
(Student Dormitory)

34:03.680 --> 34:05.720
Looks like there's no hope for recruitment.

34:06.180 --> 34:08.351
Why did I even choose this unpopular major?

34:08.651 --> 34:10.091
I'm now an unemployed graduate.

34:10.661 --> 34:11.791
I'll have to starve.

34:11.861 --> 34:14.091
There's no job to be found.

34:14.831 --> 34:17.360
When we applied for our majors back then,

34:17.501 --> 34:18.930
no one at home understood.

34:19.400 --> 34:21.171
All our hard work went to waste.

34:21.630 --> 34:23.340
We got such high scores and got into such a good university.

34:23.400 --> 34:24.340
What's the use?

34:25.240 --> 34:27.671
You choose the wrong major. There goes your life.

34:30.041 --> 34:31.811
Ye Zi. I have a high school classmate.

34:31.880 --> 34:34.450
She's working as a salesgirl at the cosmetics counter.

34:34.981 --> 34:35.911
She can do a bit of makeup too.

34:35.981 --> 34:37.220
She sells goods online.

34:37.521 --> 34:39.521
Although she doesn't have many followers,

34:39.820 --> 34:42.550
she earns at least tens of thousands a month.

34:43.021 --> 34:43.961
Unlike us.

34:44.021 --> 34:45.720
We barely make a basic of 4,000.

34:47.490 --> 34:48.791
It can't be helped.

34:49.090 --> 34:51.260
Selling goods exists at the end of the universe.

34:52.130 --> 34:53.671
But it's not that easy.

34:53.731 --> 34:55.271
Last time, I got a batch of goods.

34:55.331 --> 34:56.700
I didn't sell a single one.

34:56.840 --> 34:58.240
That's because the traffic is too low.

34:58.441 --> 35:01.041
It's better if I go door-to-door and sell them one by one.

35:01.641 --> 35:02.771
When I make my first bucket of money,

35:02.840 --> 35:04.380
I'll buy more exposure and promote myself.

35:10.010 --> 35:10.981
Ye Zi.

35:13.981 --> 35:14.751
What are you doing?

35:16.111 --> 35:17.351
You're quite photogenic.

35:18.220 --> 35:20.990
Ye Zi. Why don't I help you run an account?

35:21.251 --> 35:22.620
You can do beauty and fashion.

35:23.620 --> 35:25.791
I doubt it's as easy as you think.

35:26.061 --> 35:26.930
Give it a try.

35:26.990 --> 35:28.331
It doesn't require much anyway.

35:28.691 --> 35:29.530
Try a few more paths.

35:29.590 --> 35:31.361
What if one of them succeeds?

35:34.470 --> 35:37.340
But I got a few part-time jobs recently.

35:37.800 --> 35:38.901
You can't get in the way of my part-time jobs.

35:38.970 --> 35:41.410
Don't worry. I won't hold you back.

35:42.541 --> 35:44.510
I've discussed it with Chief Song.

35:45.510 --> 35:46.541
We've come to the same conclusion.

35:47.010 --> 35:49.651
A joint rescue team is not just about...

35:49.711 --> 35:52.021
letting the medical staff learn more about us...

35:52.081 --> 35:53.490
and cooperate with us on rescue missions.

35:53.820 --> 35:54.950
More importantly,

35:55.021 --> 35:56.720
we, the firefighters,

35:56.791 --> 35:59.090
should also know some medical knowledge.

35:59.921 --> 36:01.861
When the medical staff is unable to reach areas...

36:01.990 --> 36:04.200
that are too dangerous,

36:04.260 --> 36:06.260
we can be more efficient...

36:06.660 --> 36:08.901
in determining and providing assistance.

36:09.631 --> 36:10.570
So every day from now on,

36:10.640 --> 36:12.541
we'll set aside half a day...

36:12.941 --> 36:14.070
for the medical team...

36:14.211 --> 36:16.111
to teach us some medical knowledge.

36:16.541 --> 36:17.941
Today, Dr. Xu will teach us...

36:18.140 --> 36:20.311
some medical knowledge...

36:20.450 --> 36:22.751
that will be used...

36:22.811 --> 36:24.581
in emergency rescue procedures.

36:25.120 --> 36:26.381
- Okay. - Okay.

36:29.450 --> 36:31.160
Stopping bleeding, dressing wounds, CPR,

36:31.220 --> 36:32.120
and mouth-to-mouth resuscitation.

36:32.191 --> 36:33.120
Do you all know how to do it?

36:36.490 --> 36:37.861
The new members probably don't.

36:38.260 --> 36:40.231
The seniors can refresh what they know.

36:41.070 --> 36:42.070
We'll learn one by one.

36:42.700 --> 36:43.470
Okay.

36:43.541 --> 36:45.700
Today, we'll learn how to stop bleeding and bandage.

36:46.870 --> 36:47.671
However,

36:49.271 --> 36:50.711
I need a human model.

36:51.510 --> 36:52.581
Jiang Yi, you do it.

36:52.640 --> 36:53.311
Okay.

36:54.050 --> 36:55.251
Hang on. You're not it.

36:55.351 --> 36:57.921
Chief, Jiang Yi is not good at bandaging.

36:57.981 --> 36:59.820
You be the model.

36:59.881 --> 37:01.950
That's right, Chief. I'm not good at bandaging.

37:02.021 --> 37:03.191
I need to learn more.

37:05.461 --> 37:07.090
I'm not good at it either, Chief.

37:07.530 --> 37:08.691
Let's give him some encouragement.

37:11.101 --> 37:12.001
Okay.

37:12.061 --> 37:12.901
Go, Chief!

37:23.611 --> 37:25.541
Arterial hemorrhage is the most dangerous...

37:25.611 --> 37:27.050
among open hemorrhages.

37:27.111 --> 37:28.910
The bleeding is fast and heavy.

37:28.981 --> 37:30.111
If we don't stop the bleeding in time,

37:30.180 --> 37:31.421
it could be life-threatening.

37:31.550 --> 37:33.550
Knowing how to stop the arterial hemorrhage quickly...

37:33.620 --> 37:35.590
can buy more time for the victim to be saved.

37:36.490 --> 37:37.521
Xu Xi.

37:45.160 --> 37:46.760
When helping a patient,

37:46.901 --> 37:48.501
you can use a bandage or tourniquet...

37:48.570 --> 37:50.300
to stop the bleeding at the pericardial end of the artery.

37:51.740 --> 37:53.941
Tie the lower extremities at the mid-thigh.

37:55.410 --> 37:56.211
As for the upper extremities,

37:56.740 --> 37:57.840
tie at the lower end of the deltoid.

38:01.510 --> 38:02.450
Take a look.

38:03.921 --> 38:04.881
Right here.

38:08.090 --> 38:09.990
Chief Song, you're slacking off.

38:14.831 --> 38:15.791
Pay attention.

38:15.930 --> 38:18.700
Loosen the bandage or tourniquet every 15 minutes...

38:18.961 --> 38:20.430
to prevent ischemic necrosis.

38:25.200 --> 38:26.070
Chief.

38:28.910 --> 38:29.910
Take off your clothes.

38:31.780 --> 38:32.541
What?

38:33.410 --> 38:34.651
Take off your clothes.

38:53.300 --> 38:54.430
I'll bet you 5km...

38:54.501 --> 38:55.930
that sparks will fly between Chief and Dr. Xu.

38:56.430 --> 38:57.401
I'll bet you 10km.

38:57.470 --> 38:58.501
Before sparks fly,

38:58.570 --> 38:59.570
there will first be fire.

39:05.840 --> 39:07.381
For traumatic injuries caused by car accidents,

39:07.450 --> 39:09.111
earthquakes, or fires,

39:09.410 --> 39:11.751
the patient will often develop a high-pressure pneumothorax.

39:11.820 --> 39:13.890
If it's not punctured and vented immediately,

39:13.950 --> 39:15.191
death may be swift.

39:16.021 --> 39:16.950
Next, I'm going to talk...

39:17.021 --> 39:18.421
about the symptoms of a high-pressure pneumothorax.

39:19.861 --> 39:21.890
One, the patient has extreme breathing difficulties.

39:22.061 --> 39:24.061
In severe cases, the patient may suffocate due to hypoxia.

39:24.731 --> 39:27.370
Two, one side of the chest is swollen...

39:27.771 --> 39:29.370
and is significantly higher than the other side.

39:29.700 --> 39:30.870
As long as these two conditions are met,

39:30.941 --> 39:32.740
we need to puncture and vent immediately.

39:33.070 --> 39:34.111
In an emergency,

39:34.271 --> 39:36.410
a thick needle can be used...

39:36.570 --> 39:38.010
in the spot intersected by the second intercostal...

39:38.111 --> 39:39.211
and the midline of the clavicle...

39:39.941 --> 39:40.981
for the puncture procedure.

39:41.111 --> 39:42.180
Why don't you guys try it?

39:42.711 --> 39:43.751
Okay, I can...

39:43.981 --> 39:44.680
Not you guys.

39:46.021 --> 39:47.320
Mr. Jiang, lead the way.

39:47.390 --> 39:48.050
Okay.

39:56.430 --> 39:57.260
Hurry up.

39:58.260 --> 39:59.101
This is the first intercostal.

39:59.700 --> 40:00.731
This is the second intercostal.

40:01.101 --> 40:02.231
This is where they intersect.

40:04.901 --> 40:05.970
Very good. Next.

40:06.740 --> 40:07.541
I'll do it.

40:07.740 --> 40:09.470
Chief, excuse me.

40:11.541 --> 40:12.381
Collarbone.

40:13.541 --> 40:14.811
Here, right?

40:14.910 --> 40:15.711
This is the first rib.

40:16.180 --> 40:17.120
This is the second rib.

40:19.021 --> 40:19.780
Got it.

40:22.820 --> 40:24.590
All right. That's all for the demonstration.

40:24.820 --> 40:26.021
Chief, I haven't...

40:26.320 --> 40:27.331
Why did Chief leave?

40:27.461 --> 40:30.331
- The teaching tool is gone. - Chief Song's body is amazing.

40:30.430 --> 40:31.530
You're such a flirt.

40:31.601 --> 40:33.061
Calm down.

40:33.361 --> 40:34.930
I can't believe he ran away.

40:35.300 --> 40:36.070
Come on, Pi Pi.

40:36.131 --> 40:37.300
You be the model. Undress.

40:37.570 --> 40:38.370
No, thank you.

40:38.501 --> 40:40.300
Hurry up. A round of encouragement.
